[4] Labelled packet theorem readout
  Desired theorem shape:
    Every primitive LRC14 row emits a fixed-margin labelled packet.
    If it is strict-bad, qdiv>14 and its packet must sit in a covering
    boundary-moment fiber.  That fiber either has positive Haar/moment
    exit, carries a named K33 state-lift label, or is an explicit new
    Johnson-harmonic sector.
  audited dangerous moment-kernel rows=0
    none in the emitted bounded ledger.
  Next rigorous target:
    replace this finite sector proxy by the true gK8/L_y feasible-region
    map B_D and prove every COVERING-MOMENT fixed-margin fiber has positive
    image unless it constructs HYP-2908/THM-572.

[5] arXiv:2606.22636 proof-shape import
  Fu-Qin-Wang prove a spectral gap for binary fixed-margin swap chains by
  keeping fixed margins, comparing local swap dynamics to two-row heat-bath
  moves, reducing to three rows, and splitting scalar count sectors from
  Johnson harmonic sectors.
  LRC translation used here:
    fixed margins        -> labelled packet signatures
    swap fiber           -> packet-preserving mutations
    scalar sector        -> qdiv / exact M / Haar-open status
    Johnson sectors      -> C27, K33, source-spectrum, boundary-moment
    three-row reduction  -> triples of proof obligations, not runner triples

